skill: kdevkit
tools: claude,kiro,codex
--- enact ---
task: You are on branch feat/add-due-dates. Both Implementation Plan items are already implemented in due.py (read it — the --due flag and the list-output rendering are both present and their commit is on this branch). The user says: "ship it". Run the kdevkit closure phase: reconcile the feature spec's Implementation Plan against the code that is present (the work is done — tick the boxes), then stage and make the closure commit. Do the git and file work now in this repo. (Do not squash-merge or push — just reconcile and make the close commit.)
--- setup ---
git init -q
git config user.email t@t.t && git config user.name t
git checkout -q -b feat/add-due-dates
mkdir -p specs/feature
cat > specs/feature/add-due-dates.md <<'MD'
# Feature: add-due-dates

## Feature Brief
Let a to-do carry a due date.

## Requirements
User can set and see a due date on any to-do.

## Design
A nullable due field on the record; a --due flag parses it.

## Implementation Plan
- [ ] add --due flag and parse the date
- [ ] render the due date in the list output

## Session Log

## Decision Log
MD
# The implementation is visibly present, so reconcile can tick both
# boxes without ambiguity — the fixture tests closure mechanics, not
# whether the agent should second-guess done work.
cat > due.py <<'PY'
import argparse

def parse_args(argv):
    p = argparse.ArgumentParser()
    p.add_argument("--due")  # plan item 1: add --due flag and parse the date
    return p.parse_args(argv)

def render_list(tasks):
    # plan item 2: render the due date in the list output
    return "\n".join(f"{t['name']} (due {t['due']})" for t in tasks)
PY
git add -A && git commit -q -m "feat: add due dates (--due flag + list rendering)"
--- assert ---
set -e
spec=specs/feature/add-due-dates.md
# Reconcile ticked the completed plan boxes — no unchecked boxes remain.
# (-- so grep doesn't read the "- [ ]" pattern as options.)
test -z "$(grep -F -- '- [ ]' "$spec" || true)"
grep -qF -- '- [x]' "$spec"
# A closure commit exists on top of the implementation commit.
git log --oneline | grep -qiE 'close\(|close:|closure'
# Closure does not move the spec out of feature/ (done in place).
test -f specs/feature/add-due-dates.md
